Falsifies `extensible_host_controller_interface::verification::a_slot_context_keeps_each_field_in_its_own_bits`.

The defect: `slot` puts the speed id one bit low, at 19 to 22, so it reads back halved from its own field and its low bit lands in the reserved bit 19.

Expected to fail: the harness's check that the speed id reads back from bits 20 to 23, or that dword 0 holds nothing outside the speed and context count fields.

diff --git a/src/context.rs b/src/context.rs
--- a/src/context.rs
+++ b/src/context.rs
@@ -92,7 +92,7 @@
 #[must_use]
 pub const fn slot(speed: PortSpeed, port: PortNumber, entries: DeviceContextIndex) -> [u32; 8] {
     [
-        (speed.get() as u32) << 20 | (entries.get() as u32) << 27,
+        (speed.get() as u32) << 19 | (entries.get() as u32) << 27,
         (port.get() as u32) << 16,
         0,
         0,
